     "text": "and in speech, the supreme restraint;"
    },
    {
     "n": 13,
     "text": "happy inside, serene,"
    },
    {
     "n": 14,
     "text": "solitary, content, I call a mendicant."
    },
    {
     "n": 15,
     "text": "When a mendicant of restrained mouth,"
    },
    {
     "n": 16,
     "text": "thoughtful in counsel, not restless,"
    },
    {
     "n": 17,
     "text": "explains the text and its meaning,"
    },
    {
     "n": 18,
     "text": "their words are sweet."
    },
    {
     "n": 19,
     "text": "Delighting in the teaching, enjoying the teaching,"
    },
    {
     "n": 20,
     "text": "contemplating the teaching,"
    },
    {
     "n": 21,
     "text": "a mendicant who recollects the teaching"
    },
    {
     "n": 22,
     "text": "doesn’t fall away from the true teaching."
    },
    {
     "n": 23,
     "text": "A well-off mendicant ought not look down"
    },
    {
     "n": 24,
     "text": "on others, nor should they be envious."
    },
    {
     "n": 25,
     "text": "A mendicant who envies others"
    },
    {
     "n": 26,
     "text": "does not achieve immersion."
    },
    {
     "n": 27,
     "text": "If a mendicant is poor in offerings,"
    },
    {
     "n": 28,
     "text": "the well-to-do ought not look down on them."
    },
    {
     "n": 29,
     "text": "For the gods indeed praise them,"
    },
    {
     "n": 30,
     "text": "who are tireless and pure of livelihood."
    },
    {
     "n": 31,
     "text": "One who has no sense of ownership"
    },
    {
     "n": 32,
     "text": "in the whole realm of name and form,"
    },
    {
     "n": 33,
     "text": "who does not grieve for that which is not,"
    },
    {
     "n": 34,
     "text": "is said to be a mendicant."
    },
    {
     "n": 35,
     "text": "A mendicant who meditates on love,"
    },
    {
     "n": 36,
     "text": "devoted to the Buddha’s teaching,"
    },
    {
     "n": 37,
     "text": "would realize the peaceful state,"
    },
    {
     "n": 38,
     "text": "the blissful stilling of conditions."
    },
    {
     "n": 39,
     "text": "Bail out this boat, mendicant!"
    },
    {
     "n": 40,
     "text": "When bailed out it will float lightly."
    },
    {
     "n": 41,
     "text": "Having cut off desire and hate,"
    },
    {
     "n": 42,
     "text": "you shall reach extinguishment."
    },
    {
     "n": 43,
     "text": "Five to cut, five to drop,"
    },
    {
     "n": 44,
     "text": "and five more to develop."
    },
    {
     "n": 45,
     "text": "When a mendicant slips five chains"
    },
    {
     "n": 46,
     "text": "they’re said to have crossed the flood."
    },
    {
     "n": 47,
     "text": "Practice absorption, don’t be negligent!"
    },
    {
     "n": 48,
     "text": "Don’t let the mind delight in the senses!"
    },
    {
     "n": 49,
     "text": "Don’t heedlessly swallow a hot iron ball!"
    },
    {
     "n": 50,
     "text": "And when it burns, don’t cry, “Oh, the pain!”"
    },
    {
     "n": 51,
     "text": "No absorption for one without wisdom,"
    },
    {
     "n": 52,
     "text": "no wisdom for one without absorption."
    },
    {
     "n": 53,
     "text": "But one with absorption and wisdom—"
    },
    {
     "n": 54,
     "text": "they have truly drawn near to extinguishment."
    },
    {
     "n": 55,
     "text": "A mendicant who enters an empty hut"
    },
    {
     "n": 56,
     "text": "with mind at peace"
    },
    {
     "n": 57,
     "text": "finds a superhuman delight"
    },
    {
     "n": 58,
     "text": "as they rightly discern the Dhamma."
    },
    {
     "n": 59,
     "text": "Whenever they are mindful"
    },
    {
     "n": 60,
     "text": "of the rise and fall of the aggregates,"
    },
    {
     "n": 61,
     "text": "they feel rapture and joy:"
    },
    {
     "n": 62,
     "text": "that is freedom from death for one who knows."
    },
    {
     "n": 63,
     "text": "This is the very start of the path"
    },
    {
     "n": 64,
     "text": "for a wise mendicant here:"
    },
    {
     "n": 65,
     "text": "guarding the senses, contentment,"
    },
    {
     "n": 66,
     "text": "and restraint in the monastic code."
    },
    {
     "n": 67,
     "text": "Mix with spiritual friends,"
    },
    {
     "n": 68,
     "text": "who are tireless and pure of livelihood."
    },
    {
     "n": 69,
     "text": "Share what you have with others,"
    },
    {
     "n": 70,
     "text": "being skillful in your conduct."
    },
    {
     "n": 71,
     "text": "And when you’re full of joy,"
    },
    {
     "n": 72,
     "text": "you’ll make an end to suffering."
    },
    {
     "n": 73,
     "text": "As a jasmine sheds"
    },
    {
     "n": 74,
     "text": "its withered flowers,"
    },
    {
     "n": 75,
     "text": "O mendicants,"
    },
    {
     "n": 76,
     "text": "shed greed and hate."
    },
    {
     "n": 77,
     "text": "Calm in body, calm in speech,"
